---
import AnimatedHero from "../components/AnimatedHero.astro";
import MarketingShell from "../components/MarketingShell.astro";
---

<MarketingShell
  title="Code review that brings receipts"
  description="Warden gives your agent runtime the ground truth for code review over MCP — detectors, verified advisories, real type definitions — and publishes only what survives gates the model cannot skip."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero-section">
      <div class="hero-copy reveal-in">
        <p class="eyebrow">Review ground truth over MCP</p>
        <h1>
          Reviews with <span class="accent">receipts.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          Your agent runs the review. Warden supplies the parts it cannot make up — type errors, lint
          findings, advisories checked against OSV, real <code>.d.ts</code> signatures — and then its
          gates decide what gets published. <em>The model never gets the last word.</em>
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href="/docs/mcp/" data-astro-prefetch>
            Connect over MCP
            <span class="button-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/review/" data-astro-prefetch>How a review runs</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-meta">
          <span>Any MCP client</span>
          <span>OpenCode first</span>
          <span>Gates outside the model</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal-in delay-2">
        <AnimatedHero />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="Review contract">
      <p><strong>Runs in your repo</strong><span>a local stdio server, no hosted backend, no upload</span></p>
      <p><strong>Any MCP client</strong><span>OpenCode is the first client, not a dependency</span></p>
      <p><strong>Gates are not tools</strong><span>verification runs after the model, every time</span></p>
      <p><strong>Measured, not vibed</strong><span>recall and precision evals gate each change</span></p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-band">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The split</p>
        <h2>The loop is a commodity. The evidence is <span class="accent">not.</span></h2>
        <p class="section-sub">
          Agent runtimes get better at sub-agents, model routing, and permissions with every release.
          None of them ships a detector corpus, verified advisories, or a repo index. So Warden stopped
          running the loop and kept the parts that have to be right.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="feature-kicker">01 · EVIDENCE</span>
          <h3>Ground truth, <em>over MCP.</em></h3>
          <p>
            <code>run_det_priors</code> returns TSC, ESLint, npm audit with OSV, duplication, security
            lint, and context selection as a bounded, versioned, paged bundle.
            <code>lookup_type_def</code> answers library API questions from installed type
            definitions.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="feature-kicker">02 · LANES</span>
          <h3>Your runtime does <em>the reading.</em></h3>
          <p>
            Review lanes run as agents in your client, with read-only tools. The down lane traces a
            claimed behavior through callers, state, and failure paths. The up lane looks for
            structural drift.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="feature-kicker">03 · POST-PASS</span>
          <h3>Gates the model <em>can't skip.</em></h3>
          <p>
            A model can decline to call a tool, so verification is not a tool. After the lanes return,
            Warden checks every citation, scopes findings to the diff, screens secrets, applies the
            confidence and volume rules, and emits the <code>CommentSet</code>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="workflow-band">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">How a review runs</p>
        <h2>Evidence in, receipts <span class="accent">out.</span></h2>
        <p class="section-sub">
          <code>warden opencode-review</code> drives the whole path: it starts the MCP server, runs a
          lane in OpenCode, and publishes only what the post-pass returns. Lane prose never reaches
          you directly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="review-spine">
        <li>
          <span>Diff</span>
          <em class="spine-status">shipped</em>
          <p>Resolve the base by merge-base, prune generated files, and stop before spawn on unsafe input such as a symlink that leaves the repo.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Det-priors</span>
          <em class="spine-status">shipped</em>
          <p>The lane calls <code>run_det_priors</code> first and reads the findings page by page, by handle, without flooding its context.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Lanes</span>
          <em class="spine-status partial">partial</em>
          <p>Down proves invariants. Up searches for structural drift and is opt-in. Surface and judge come next.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Post-pass</span>
          <em class="spine-status">shipped</em>
          <p>Verify citations, keep each finding inside its lane's file scope, demote by confidence, and cap volume. Tier 1 always survives the cap.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>Publish</span>
          <em class="spine-status">shipped</em>
          <p>Emit one stable <code>CommentSet</code>. The trusted scope envelope comes from the driver, never from the model.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <div class="review-boundary" role="note">
        <strong>Mid-pivot, said out loud.</strong>
        <p>
          <code>warden review</code> still runs the original in-process boss loop, and it stays the
          default until the parity eval shows the MCP path matches it on recall and precision. The CI
          runner is a tracer today: it writes to the job summary and does not comment on PRs yet.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="connect-band">
      <div class="section-heading connect-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Connect</p>
        <h2>One server. Any <span class="accent">client.</span></h2>
        <p class="section-sub">
          <code>warden mcp</code> speaks JSON-RPC over stdio and nothing else. Every result carries a
          schema version, stays under a size bound, and degrades to a structured reason instead of
          throwing.
        </p>
        <ul class="connect-facts">
          <li><code>run_det_priors</code><span>the deterministic evidence bundle, paged</span></li>
          <li><code>lookup_type_def</code><span>library API signatures from installed <code>.d.ts</code></span></li>
          <li><code>search_index</code><span>semantic repo search, next</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal-window connect-code">
        <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="dot"></span>
          <span class="dot"></span>
          <span class="dot"></span>
          <span class="terminal-title">opencode.jsonc</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="terminal-body"><code><span class="tok-punct">&#123;</span>
  <span class="tok-key">"mcp"</span><span class="tok-punct">: &#123;</span>
    <span class="tok-key">"servers"</span><span class="tok-punct">: &#123;</span>
      <span class="tok-key">"warden"</span><span class="tok-punct">: &#123;</span>
        <span class="tok-key">"type"</span><span class="tok-punct">:</span> <span class="tok-str">"local"</span><span class="tok-punct">,</span>
        <span class="tok-key">"command"</span><span class="tok-punct">: [</span><span class="tok-str">"warden"</span><span class="tok-punct">,</span> <span class="tok-str">"mcp"</span><span class="tok-punct">]</span>
      <span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span>
    <span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span>
  <span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span>
<span class="tok-punct">&#125;</span></code></pre>
        <p class="connect-note">
          Warden is not on npm yet. Point <code>command</code> at a local checkout —
          <a href="/docs/mcp/" data-astro-prefetch>the docs show the exact form</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="anatomy-band">
      <div class="anatomy-wrap">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Anatomy</p>
          <h2>What lands in a <span class="accent">comment.</span></h2>
          <p class="section-sub">
            Every Warden comment is a small receipt: a tiered claim, a category, a confidence
            number, the lane that found it, and the sources that earned it the right to interrupt
            you.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="anatomy-key">Tier</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Block · Fix · Consider</strong>
                <p>Three steps of actionability, never inflated. Tier 1 is what would block a merge.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="anatomy-key">Category</span>
              <div>
                <strong>correctness, security, scalability, …</strong>
                <p>Reading order, not severity. The six concerns are focus areas inside a lane, not lanes of their own.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="anatomy-key">Sources</span>
              <div>
                <strong>Path, line, snippet — verified</strong>
                <p>Every external claim points at a real artifact. The post-pass substring-matches it before the comment ships.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="anatomy-key">Degraded</span>
              <div>
                <strong>What didn't run, said out loud</strong>
                <p>If a lane or a detector fails, the run admits it. Silence is the failure mode Warden refuses.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <aside class="receipt" aria-label="Sample comment receipt">
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span class="receipt-key">id</span>
            <span class="receipt-val">w-7c8f3a · stable across runs</span>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span class="receipt-key">tier</span>
            <span class="receipt-val tier-1">1 · Block</span>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span class="receipt-key">lane</span>
            <span class="receipt-val">down · correctness</span>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span class="receipt-key">confidence</span>
            <span class="receipt-val">96%</span>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span class="receipt-key">file</span>
            <span class="receipt-val">src/routes/session.ts:88</span>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span class="receipt-key">claim</span>
            <span class="receipt-val">
              <span class="receipt-emph">exec</span> receives request-controlled input before validation.
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-row">
            <span class="receipt-key">source</span>
            <span class="receipt-val">security/detect-child-process · tool</span>
          </div>
          <div class="receipt-quote">
            child_process.exec(req.query.command)
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-band">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Design record</p>
        <h2>Every choice is <span class="accent">written down.</span></h2>
        <p>
          More than fifty ADRs record what Warden does, what it refused, and why. ADR-0053 is the one
          behind this page: keep the method and the gates, hand the loop to a runtime that does it
          better.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="closing-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/99Yash/warden/blob/main/decisions.md" rel="noreferrer">Read the decisions</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/notes/" data-astro-prefetch>Field notes</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</MarketingShell>
